## INTEGRATION FLOW

### 1. Importing Types
```typescript
import { CaptionWord, WordStyleOverrides, CaptionItemData } from '../store/types';
```

### 2. Getting the Action
```typescript
import { useEditorActions } from '../store/use-editor-store';

function MyComponent\(\) {
  const { updateWordStyleOverrides } = useEditorActions\(\);
  // ...
}
```

### 3. Calling the Action
```typescript
// Simple override
updateWordStyleOverrides\(captionId, wordIndex, {
  color: '#ff0000',
}\);

// Multiple overrides
updateWordStyleOverrides\(captionId, wordIndex, {
  color: '#ff0000',
  fontWeight: 900,
  scale: 1.2,
  emphasisBg: '#ffff00',
}\);

// Partial update \(merges\)
updateWordStyleOverrides\(captionId, wordIndex, {
  color: '#00ff00',
}\);

// Clear all
updateWordStyleOverrides\(captionId, wordIndex, null\);
```

### 4. In the Renderer
The renderer automatically reads `word.styleOverrides` from the CaptionWord object and applies it to the final CSS styles.

